4. Official copies

An “official copy” is a DebArk distribution whose files and release metadata
match a release signed by the official DebArk signing key. A copied or
repackaged distribution is official only while its covered files and signed
metadata remain unchanged. A cryptographic signature verifies the origin and
integrity of a release; it does not make modified code impossible to produce.

